# Supply Chain

This is the documentation of the SquirrelJME supply chain. Effectively, this
is the list of projects, services, and otherwise that are hard and/or soft
dependencies that the project relies upon for existing. This only includes
direct proper noun dependencies or direct pseudo dependencies that are
needed to build SquirrelJME.

This does not include obvious things such as an internet connection, package
repositories, developers, or operating systems.

SquirrelJME has the goal to be as self-hosted and self-reliable as possible,
it is a preservation platform.

 * [Apache Commons Collections 4](
https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-collections/) (Building)
   * Version: 4.5.0-M3 (December 19, 2024)
   * AI Usage: None could be found for this version.
 * _C Compiler_ (Building)
   * Minimum Version: C89 (December 14, 1989)
   * AI Usage: As this is a standardized language, the consensus is that
     since 2024 any MSVC, GCC, and/or LLVM based compiler has extensively used
     AI for development.
 * [CMake](https://cmake.org/) (Building)
   * Minimum Version: 3.1 (December 17, 2014)
   * Maximum Version: 3.31 (November 7, 2024)
   * AI Usage: Very possible with the later sub-releases of 3.31 as Kitware
     is quoted "A Trusted Partner for Custom Software and Advanced AI
     Research". Any version at least 4.0 has development history that
     extensively uses AI.
 * [Fossil](https://www.fossil-scm.org/) (Version Control)
   * This is for source control and history, the project does not rely upon it
     to exist and can work off extracted source archives. If you have the
     source code you do not need Fossil, just that you will lose out on getting
     the commit hash for the version number.
   * Minimum Tested Version: 1.28 (January 27, 2014)
   * AI Usage: Any version released since 2026, the exact quantity is unknown.
 * [Gradle](https://gradle.com/) (Building)
   * Version: 7.6.6 (July 4, 2025)
   * AI Usage: Possible for 7.6.6 although this is a minor update to an
     unsupported Gradle version at the time. Newer versions are developed with
     AI extensively as Develocity is quoted "Give AI the context to deliver
     software, with Governance and Efficiency". Newer versions extensively
     use AI for development.
 * IBan4J (Building)
   * The original website for the project is no longer online.
   * Version: 3.27 (September 30, 2023)
   * AI Usage: None. Project ownership has since been transferred of which
     the developers utilize AI extensively for development.
 * [Install4J](https://www.ej-technologies.com/install4j) (Snapshots)
   * This is not strictly needed, however it provides convenient installers
     which are simple and easy to use.
   * Version: 12 (October 31, 2025)
   * AI Usage: Unknown for this version, this is a closed-source commercial
     product. Install4J 13 includes an "AI agent skill" along with other
     AI integration, thus it is extremely likely that it is
     utilizing AI in development.
 * [Jasmin](https://jasmin.sourceforge.net/) (Building)
   * Version: 3.0.3 (December 29, 2021)
   * AI Usage: None.
 * _Java Compiler_ (Building)
   * Minimum Version: 1.8 (March 18, 2014)
   * AI Usage: None for this version, however any release since 2024 has used
     AI in bug discovery. OpenJDK's interim policy as of this writing only
     permits bug discovery and not code generation.
 * [OpenCSV](https://opencsv.sourceforge.net/) (Building)
   * Version: 5.10 (January 12, 2025)
   * AI Usage: None could be found for this version, it is very unlikely as
     this is a project which has a single purpose and is effectively complete.
 * [ProGuard](https://www.guardsquare.com/proguard) (Building)
   * This is not strictly needed, it is intended to be used to shrink the
     resultant Jars as much as possible.
   * Version: 7.3.2 (March 17, 2023)
   * AI Usage: None could be found for this version. For newer versions this
     is unknown, there is no indication that it has been adopted.
 * [Project Lombok](https://projectlombok.org/) (Building)
   * Version: 1.18.36 (November 15, 2024)
   * AI Usage: None could be found for this version. For newer versions it is
     unlikely unless a passerby contributor has lied about via AI. The current
     maintainers of the project are openly hostile to AI, users of AI,
     companies that use AI, the companies that control the entirety of
     the AI market, and the products/services they use being destroyed by AI.
 * Shadow Jar (Building)
   * This is not strictly needed, it is only used to build the Standalone
     variant of Hosted and SpringCoat.
   * The original website for the project is no longer online.
   * Version: 7.1.2 (December 29, 2021)
   * AI Usage: None for this version. Project ownership has since been
     transferred to GradleUp, which extensively utilizes AI.
